From 0eeff296ea995113b98f11ea92df696783932dba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:52:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 093/240] Bugfix: do not split contexts in nested dissection
 ordering when deterministic behavior is wanted [report PyScotch]

`hgraphOrderNd()` and `hmeshOrderNd()` split the execution context in
two whenever at least two threads are available. The second
sub-context receives a new pseudo-random generator, so that the
pseudo-random sequences consumed by the recursion depend on the number
of threads, and orderings differ between runs with 1, 2 or 4 threads
even when the deterministic option is set, while the documentation
states that this option yields the same results for any number of
threads.
Run the two sub-tasks in sequence, within the same context, when
deterministic behavior is wanted, as `graphMatchInit()` does for
threaded matching and as `kgraphMapRbPart2()` does for recursive
bipartitioning.

Refs: PS2-G08-2
---
 src/libscotch/hgraph_order_nd.c | 12 +++++++++---
 src/libscotch/hmesh_order_nd.c  | 12 +++++++++---
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/hgraph_order_nd.c b/src/libscotch/hgraph_order_nd.c
